From: Waltteri Hooli <waltteri.hooli@nortal.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: cq8725s-ayn: drop the SS redriver, fix the QMP PHY supplies

Two Type-C fixes on top of the vendored Odin 3 tree (9000):

- The NB7VPQ904M at i2c 0x1c never acks: plugging a USB-C hub logs a burst
  of "geni_i2c a94000.i2c: GPI transfer failed: -5" and the hub never
  enumerates. Route the connector's SS port straight to the QMP PHY again and
  disable the redriver node. With that the hub enumerates and DP AUX reads the
  sink's DPCD. Verified on hardware 2026-10-21.

- usb_dp_qmpphy had vdda-phy and vdda-pll swapped (1.2 V on phy, 0.88 V on
  pll). Same fix as armada-os/armada#722, "fix the swapped USB QMP PHY
  supplies".

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi	2026-10-21 17:43:17.525200529 +0300
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/cq8725s-ayn-common.dtsi	2026-10-21 17:43:17.542859577 +0300
@@ -231,7 +231,7 @@
 					reg = <1>;
 
 					pmic_glink_ss_in: endpoint {
-						remote-endpoint = <&redriver_ss_out>;
+						remote-endpoint = <&usb_dp_qmpphy_out>;
 					};
 				};
 
@@ -907,9 +907,16 @@
 		sound-name-prefix = "SPK_R";
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Out of the Type-C graph and disabled: it never acks on this bus (every
+	 * write fails with -EIO), and with it in the SS path a USB-C hub never
+	 * enumerates. Without it the hub does, and AUX reads the sink's DPCD.
+	 * Revisit if an enable GPIO for it turns up.
+	 */
 	typec_mux_redriver: typec-mux@1c {
 		compatible = "onnn,nb7vpq904m";
 		reg = <0x1c>;
+		status = "disabled";
 
 		vcc-supply = <&vreg_l15b_1p8>;
 
@@ -1448,8 +1455,8 @@
 };
 
 &usb_dp_qmpphy {
-	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l3g_1p2>;
-	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l2d_0p88>;
+	vdda-phy-supply = <&vreg_l2d_0p88>;
+	vdda-pll-supply = <&vreg_l3g_1p2>;
 
 	mode-switch;
 
@@ -1457,7 +1464,7 @@
 };
 
 &usb_dp_qmpphy_out {
-	remote-endpoint = <&redriver_ss_in>;
+	remote-endpoint = <&pmic_glink_ss_in>;
 };
 
 &usb_dwc3_hs {
